## Fix 1 (H1): misplaced doc comment
`internal/config/config_test.go` lines 11-23: the split left isolateConfig's nine-line doc comment glued onto clearBeadsEnv's comment, and isolateConfig (line ~40) has none. Move the isolateConfig paragraph to sit directly above `func isolateConfig`; leave clearBeadsEnv with only its own five lines. Run gofmt.

## Fix 2 (H2): runBDBinary passes the host's BD_*/BEADS_* env to the child bd
`cmd/bd/claim_test.go:288 runBDBinary` builds the child env as `append(os.Environ(), env...)`, so a host `BD_JSON=true` flips the spawned bd to JSON output and both claim tests fail on the literal "Claimed issue". Two per-test pins (BEADS_NO_DAEMON=0, BD_NO_DAEMON=false) already exist because of the same passthrough. Fix the cause once: in runBDBinary, filter every `BD_*` and `BEADS_*` entry out of `os.Environ()` before appending the per-test `env` overrides, with a two-line comment saying why. Then remove the now-redundant `BD_NO_DAEMON=false` pin at ~line 414 only if the test still passes without it under `BD_NO_DAEMON=true` exported; otherwise keep it and say so in the report.

## Fix 3 (H3): the cross-prefix skip in upsertIssues is silent
`internal/importer/importer.go` ~line 644, the `!sameProject` branch does only `result.Skipped++`. Add one `fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, ...)` line before it naming `existing.ID`, `incoming.ID` and the configured prefix, in the style of the tombstone message at ~line 262 ("Ignoring prefix mismatches ..."), e.g. `Skipping %s: same content as %s but not a rename within prefix '%s'`. When configuredPrefix is empty, name the two IDs' own prefixes instead. Nothing else changes in that function.

